eliasshub.1249

The strategies of the players are:

1)"whatever": This player takes a random coordinates (x, y) and then add a Mark in this
 coordinates on the board.
 If the coordinates are illegal (putMark returns false), he takes a new random (x, y).
 He continues like this until he gets legal ones.

2)"clever": This player loops through the rows of the board, in each row he moves from left to right,
 until he finds an empty box to add the Mark in it. 
 He wins most of the games against "whatever" because he adds the marks in one direction so he reaches
 WIN_STREAK faster.

3)"snartypamts": This player loops through the columns of the board, starting from the second column.
 In each column, he moves from top to bottom, until he finds an empty box to add the Mark in it.
 He wins most of the games against "whatever" because he adds the Marks in 
 one direction. 
 He wins most of the games against "clever" because he starts filling Marks from the second column, 
 so he interrupts the streak that "clever" will reach (because clever starts filling from the first row), 
 so that "clever" will need one more Mark to add to win. So snartypamts will reach the streak before.

Results of Tournaments of 500 games with SIZE = 6, WIN_STREAK = 4:

1)between "clever" and "whatever": 
 "clever" wins: 471, "whatever" wins: 29, draws: 0.

2)between "snartypamts" and "whatever": 
 "snartypamts" wins: 482, "whatever" wins: 18, draws: 0.

3)between "snartypamts" and "clever": 
 "snartypamts" wins: 500, "clever" wins: 0, draws: 0.

Result of Tournaments of 10000 games between two "whatever" players with SIZE = 6, WIN_STRAK = 4:

Player 1 wins: 4970, Player 2: 4976, draws: 54.

			
             